# One-shot versus shared live UI

**One-shot `@post:fragment`:** the acting tab morphs. A second tab stays stale until it
clicks or reloads. That is the correct default (the [counter](/examples/counter/)).

**Shared `@get:live(path)`:** the generated path polls; unchanged HTML is skipped.
Every open tab morphs the region. Use it when two clients must see the same
HTML without a full reload (the [live counter](/examples/live-counter/)).

Cost: every subscribed stream adds a connection and polling work. Prefer one
coherence stream per page. A module with exactly one stream gets automatic
body injection; multiple streams require explicit subscriptions and make the
cost visible. App-wide method/path collisions are rejected.

**Related:** [Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).
